IMPORT prelude

-- Audit Act 1966 (Singapore) -- whose accounts the Auditor-General must audit and who pays (ss 3, 4), the "follow-the-dollar" audit
-- of a private individual or business that takes a grant, supplies goods or services, or handles money for the State (s 4A), the
-- powers to enter and seize (s 6(1)(b), (d)), the duty to answer and the privileges that do not excuse it (ss 6(7), 6A, 7(1), (2)),
-- what the Auditor-General may pass on (s 7(3), (4)), and the reporting deadlines (s 8(2)-(4)).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/AA1966.txt. The deposit says the revised edition
-- "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on 31 December 2021"; the latest
-- amending Act annotated in the text and listed in the Legislative History is Act 42 of 2017 (Audit (Amendment) Act 2017, in force
-- 1 November 2017). The source metadata records the version as current at 1 October 2026.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0159 in subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl: Tier 3 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. It asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked a sharper
-- question yet. The Act is short (ss 1-9), so the scope is most of it, read from the side of the person or business that meets the
-- Auditor-General: chiefly the recipient of a grant, a government supplier or subcontractor, and anyone asked for documents.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: s 2 definitions beyond their use below; s 3(2)-(4) access and further duties; s 5 (what the audit examines) except as
-- the subject of s 4A(2); s 6(1)(a), (c), (e)-(g), 6(2)-(5) beyond the production notice; s 6A(3); s 8(1), (5)-(9) except s 8(4);
-- s 9 regulations (none retrieved). The Act creates no offence and no penalty of its own for refusing to answer (see NOTES.md).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text, following the conventions of the example rows (the writing-l4-rules skill was not
-- available in this session). No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. NOT for public use. See NOTES.md.

§ `Audit Act 1966 -- audits`

§§ `3 and 4 -- whose accounts must be audited, and the fee`

-- s 3(1): "The accounts of all departments and offices of the Government (including the office of the Public Service Commission) and
-- the accounts of the Supreme Court, all subordinate courts and Parliament must be audited and reported on by the Auditor-General."
-- s 4(1): the Auditor-General must "(a) if it is so provided by any written law -- audit the accounts of any public authority; and
-- (b) if it is not so provided by any written law -- with the Minister's consent if so requested by a public authority or a body
-- administering public funds, audit the accounts of such public authority or body."
-- s 4(4): "Despite any written law relating to the accounts and audit of any public authority, the Minister may, if the Minister is
-- satisfied that the public interest so requires, direct that the accounts of the authority must be audited by the Auditor-General."
-- s 2: "public authority" means the President, the Government, any statutory authority, any tribunal other than the Supreme Court and
-- the subordinate courts, or any officer or authority acting for them. A charity administering donated moneys is treated below as a
-- "body administering public funds" that is not a public authority (an inference from the s 2 definition of "public funds").
DECLARE Entity IS ONE OF
    `a government department`
    `the Public Service Commission`
    `the Supreme Court`
    `a subordinate court`
    `Parliament`
    `a statutory board`
    `a charity administering public funds`
    `a private company`

GIVEN `the entity` IS AN Entity
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the entity is audited under section 3` IF
    CONSIDER `the entity`
    WHEN `a government department` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the Public Service Commission` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the Supreme Court` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a subordinate court` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Parliament` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the entity` IS AN Entity,
      `a written law provides for the audit` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the entity requested the audit` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the Minister consented` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the Minister directed it in the public interest` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Auditor-General must audit the accounts` IF
    CONSIDER `the entity`
    WHEN `a statutory board` THEN
            `a written law provides for the audit`
        OR  (`the entity requested the audit` AND `the Minister consented`)
        OR  `the Minister directed it in the public interest`
    WHEN `a charity administering public funds` THEN `the entity requested the audit` AND `the Minister consented`
    WHEN `a private company` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 4(2): "The fee for any audit under subsection (1) is a charge upon the funds of the public authority or body concerned."
-- (3): the fee is determined by the Minister unless otherwise determined under another written law.
-- (5): "No fee is payable for an audit directed in accordance with subsection (4)."
-- The Act says nothing about a fee for the s 3 audits; this encoding treats no fee as charged under this Act for them (inference).
GIVEN `the entity` IS AN Entity,
      `a written law provides for the audit` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the entity requested the audit` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the Minister consented` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the Minister directed it in the public interest` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the entity pays a fee under section 4` IF
        (NOT `the entity is audited under section 3` `the entity`)
    AND (NOT `the Minister directed it in the public interest`)
    AND `the Auditor-General must audit the accounts` `the entity` `a written law provides for the audit` `the entity requested the audit` `the Minister consented` `the Minister directed it in the public interest`

§§ `4A -- follow-the-dollar audits of an individual or business`

-- s 4A(1): the Auditor-General may audit and report on "an individual or a person" in relation to -- (a) the giving by any public
-- authority, the Supreme Court, any subordinate court or Parliament of (i) "a grant, a subsidy, an advance of money or a loan, a
-- guarantee for the performance of an obligation or an indemnity" or (ii) "financial assistance as a result of the taking of an
-- interest in any property or person"; (b) "a supply of any goods or services (or both) under an agreement to which any public
-- authority ... is party, or under a relevant subcontract"; (c) "the collection or disbursement of money for or on behalf of" any of
-- them.
-- s 4A(2): the audit "must be limited to whether the terms and conditions applicable ... have been complied with", and (2)(b) speaks of
-- "a supply BY an individual or person". Buying from the State is therefore treated as outside s 4A (a reading of (1)(b) with (2)(b)).
-- s 4A(3): the audit "may be undertaken by the Auditor-General only if the Minister, where satisfied that it is in the public interest
-- ..., directs the Auditor-General to undertake the audit".
DECLARE Dealing IS ONE OF
    `a grant`
    `a subsidy`
    `an advance of money or a loan`
    `a guarantee or an indemnity`
    `financial assistance by taking an interest`
    `a supply of goods or services under an agreement`
    `a supply under a relevant subcontract`
    `collecting or disbursing money on its behalf`
    `buying goods or services from it`
    `a donation to it`
    `paying tax to it`

DECLARE Giver IS ONE OF
    `the Government`
    `a statutory authority`
    `the Supreme Court`
    `a subordinate court`
    `Parliament`
    `a charity that is not a public authority`
    `a private company`

GIVEN `the dealing` IS A Dealing
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the dealing is within section 4A(1)` IF
    CONSIDER `the dealing`
    WHEN `buying goods or services from it` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a donation to it` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `paying tax to it` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the giver` IS A Giver
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the other party is within section 4A(1)` IF
    CONSIDER `the giver`
    WHEN `a charity that is not a public authority` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a private company` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 4A(4): a contract is a relevant subcontract "if the performance of the contract fulfils, or contributes to the fulfilment of, an
-- obligation to supply any goods or services (or both) to the public authority ... in another contract".
GIVEN `the subcontract feeds a supply owed to a public body under another contract` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the contract is a relevant subcontract` IF `the subcontract feeds a supply owed to a public body under another contract`

GIVEN `the dealing` IS A Dealing, `the giver` IS A Giver, `the Minister directed the audit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Auditor-General may audit the individual or business` IF
        `the dealing is within section 4A(1)` `the dealing`
    AND `the other party is within section 4A(1)` `the giver`
    AND `the Minister directed the audit`

-- s 4A(2) and s 5(2): the audit asks whether the terms and conditions of the grant, supply, or collection or disbursement were
-- complied with -- and nothing else.
DECLARE Question IS ONE OF
    `whether the terms and conditions of the dealing were complied with`
    `the business's unrelated contracts`
    `the business's general finances`

GIVEN `the question` IS A Question
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the question is within a section 4A audit` IF
    CONSIDER `the question`
    WHEN `whether the terms and conditions of the dealing were complied with` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `6(1)(b) and (d) -- entry and seizure`

-- s 6(1)(b): the Auditor-General may enter, remain on and search premises "(i) occupied by any public authority, the Supreme Court, any
-- subordinate court or Parliament; (ii) occupied by any individual or person subject to an audit under section 4A; or (iii) occupied
-- by the other person ... with whom [such a body or person] has an arrangement to have possession or custody of any record,
-- information or document belonging to" it. s 6(5): "without payment".
DECLARE Occupier IS ONE OF
    `a public authority`
    `a court or Parliament`
    `a person under a section 4A audit`
    `a custodian holding records for an audited body or person`
    `an unconnected private person`

GIVEN `the occupier` IS AN Occupier
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Auditor-General may enter the premises` IF
    CONSIDER `the occupier`
    WHEN `an unconnected private person` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 6(1)(d): may seize anything in those premises if "(i) a notice under subsection (2)(a) has been given in respect of the record,
-- information or document and the period mentioned in that notice has expired; or (ii) the Auditor-General considers it necessary to
-- do so for the purpose of obtaining evidence of the contravention of any written law".
GIVEN `the occupier` IS AN Occupier,
      `a production notice was given for it` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the notice period has expired` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `seizure is considered necessary for evidence of a contravention` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Auditor-General may seize it` IF
        `the Auditor-General may enter the premises` `the occupier`
    AND (   (`a production notice was given for it` AND `the notice period has expired`)
         OR `seizure is considered necessary for evidence of a contravention`)

§§ `6(6), 6(7), 6A and 7(1), (2) -- the duty to answer`

-- s 6(7): "Any person who is required by the Auditor-General, or a person or public officer authorised under subsection (6), to provide
-- any explanation or information, produce any record, information or document or answer any question must provide [it]". s 6(6): the
-- powers "may be exercised by any public officer authorised in writing ... by the Auditor-General or by any other person so authorised".
DECLARE Requester IS ONE OF
    `the Auditor-General`
    `a public officer authorised in writing`
    `another person authorised in writing`
    `an official without written authority`

GIVEN `the requester` IS A Requester
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person must answer` IF
    CONSIDER `the requester`
    WHEN `an official without written authority` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 6A(1): an individual "cannot rely on (a) the common law privilege against self-incrimination or exposure to the imposition of a
-- penalty; or (b) any rule of law relating to legal professional privilege or any other privilege, or the public interest" to refuse.
-- s 7(1): s 6 "is not limited by any provision (including a provision relating to secrecy) contained in any other written law except
-- to the extent to which any such other written law expressly excludes the operation of that section". s 7(2): despite "the making of
-- an oath or declaration of secrecy", no offence or financial penalty "by reason of anything done by the person for the purposes of
-- section 6".
DECLARE Ground IS ONE OF
    `the privilege against self-incrimination`
    `exposure to a penalty`
    `legal professional privilege`
    `another privilege`
    `the public interest`
    `a secrecy provision in another written law`
    `an oath of secrecy`
    `another written law that expressly excludes section 6`

GIVEN `the ground` IS A Ground
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the ground excuses refusing to answer` IF
    CONSIDER `the ground`
    WHEN `another written law that expressly excludes section 6` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `done for the purposes of section 6` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is liable for breaching secrecy` IF NOT `done for the purposes of section 6`

-- s 6A(2): what is obtained because of the answer, or the fact of production or the answer, "is not admissible in evidence against the
-- individual in any civil or criminal proceeding other than a proceeding for an offence under section 177 of the Penal Code 1871 or an
-- offence relating to the falsity of the answer, if the explanation, information or answer ... might in fact tend to incriminate the
-- individual." The protection is for an individual; companies are not encoded.
DECLARE Proceeding IS ONE OF
    `a civil proceeding`
    `a prosecution for another offence`
    `a prosecution under section 177 of the Penal Code 1871`
    `a prosecution for the falsity of the answer`

GIVEN `the proceeding` IS A Proceeding, `the answer might tend to incriminate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the answer is admissible against the individual` IF
        (NOT `the answer might tend to incriminate`)
    OR  CONSIDER `the proceeding`
        WHEN `a prosecution under section 177 of the Penal Code 1871` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `a prosecution for the falsity of the answer` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `7(3) and (4) -- what the Auditor-General may pass on`

-- s 7(3): the Auditor-General "or any other person must not divulge or communicate, except, in the course of duty, to another person
-- performing duties under this Act, any information" obtained under s 6 where the source "could not, but for the provisions of this
-- Act, lawfully have divulged that information". (4): this "does not prevent the making, divulging or communicating in any report of
-- the Auditor-General of conclusions, observations or recommendations which are based on" it. Raw information in a report is not
-- named in (4); this encoding treats it as barred (a reading).
DECLARE Disclosure IS ONE OF
    `to a colleague performing duties under the Act`
    `conclusions or recommendations in an Auditor-General report`
    `the raw information in an Auditor-General report`
    `to the press`
    `to another government agency`

GIVEN `the disclosure` IS A Disclosure, `the source could lawfully have divulged it anyway` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the disclosure is permitted` IF
        `the source could lawfully have divulged it anyway`
    OR  CONSIDER `the disclosure`
        WHEN `to a colleague performing duties under the Act` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `conclusions or recommendations in an Auditor-General report` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `8(2)-(4) -- reporting deadlines`

-- s 8(2): if the Minister's statement under s 18 of the Financial Procedure Act 1966 is "not being received within a period of 7 months
-- after the close of the financial year", the Auditor-General "must submit a report to that effect to the President".
GIVEN `the statement has been received` IS A BOOLEAN, `months since the financial year closed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Auditor-General must report the missing statement` IF
    (NOT `the statement has been received`) AND `months since the financial year closed` GREATER THAN 7

-- s 8(3): the President "must present the report and statement to Parliament within 30 days of their receipt by him or her, or if
-- Parliament is not in session, within 14 days after the commencement of its next sitting". Days are counted as day numbers.
GIVEN `Parliament is in session` IS A BOOLEAN, `day of receipt` IS A NUMBER, `day the next sitting commences` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the last day to present the report` MEANS
    IF `Parliament is in session` THEN `day of receipt` PLUS 30
    ELSE `day the next sitting commences` PLUS 14

-- s 8(4): nothing in (3) requires presentation of any matter which "the Prime Minister and the Minister responsible for defence, on the
-- recommendations of the Permanent Secretary to the Ministry of Defence and the Chief of Defence Force, certify to be necessary for the
-- defence and security of Singapore". (5): the certificate is "conclusive evidence".
GIVEN `certified as necessary for defence and security` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the matter must be presented to Parliament` IF NOT `certified as necessary for defence and security`
